 | Pixel buffers everywhere | [Pixel buffers](architecture/images.md#pixel-buffers), [#107](https://github.com/nsgo-dev/nsgo/issues/107), [#1101](https://github.com/nsgo-dev/nsgo/issues/1101) | Measure frame continuity and cost at 960×540 and 1920×1080 at 60 fps on macOS, Windows and Linux, and at 1920×1080 on Android. Skip copies for hidden and minimized windows. Give QQ, Douyin and Alipay a canvas binding for image views. Verify that a `Shader` shows each version of a 960×540 texture rewritten at 60 fps without blank frames on macOS, iOS, Windows, Linux, Android and the web. Android and the web have 960×540 frame captures and timing measurements. Headless checks cover Apple image views, Metal texture uploads and Linux drawing. WeChat Developer Tools verified pixel images and draws of offscreen buffers. A HarmonyOS device showed each version of a buffer rewritten each frame in an image view and a canvas, and its per-frame cost is recorded. Shader frames at 960×540 were checked on macOS, an iOS simulator, Android, Chrome, Linux's llvmpipe and Windows CI (#1115), and the Pixel 3 XL's pipe cost for them is recorded. [Performance](architecture/performance.md#keeping-frames-cheap) |
